  "comments": "The 2008 strike was released as part of the changeover from the Emblems of Britain to the Royal Shield. The coin was also issued in copper-nickel, silver piedfort, gold proof and platinum proof. Issue Limit: 10,000<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/604d1799e20d3.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/604d1799e20d3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"216\" /></a><br />\r\n© The Royal Mint, 2008<br /><br />\r\nIn 2011, Spink changed their reference number for this coin when the composition of the base metal strike changed to Ni plated steel:<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Sp#F6</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(2008-11)</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Sp#F7</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(2012-15)</span><br /><br />\r\nIn 2012, for the Queen&#039;s Diamond Jubilee most coins were selectively plated with Gold and so this silver proof edition was limited.<br /><br />\r\nThe 2015 strike was issued as part of the dual set to commemorate the change from the 4th portrait to the 5th and was also struck in copper-nickel, gold proof and platinum proof.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/604d17d25a0ed.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/604d17d25a0ed.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"206\" /></a><br />\r\n© The Royal Mint, 2008<br /><br />\r\n2008 issue limit: 10,000<br />\r\n2009 issue limit: 7,500<br />\r\n2010 issue limit: 3,500<br />\r\n2011 issue limit: 2,500<br />\r\n2012 issue limit: 995<br />\r\n2013 issue limit: 2,013<br />\r\n2014 issue limit: 2,014<br />\r\n2015 issue limit: 7,500",
